nixarchy #1192: a panel that fails to load says why.

CARRIED: the panel Loader's onStatusChanged called `errorString &&
errorString()`, but Qt 6's Loader has no errorString(), so a failed panel
logged "ReferenceError: errorString is not defined" instead of its real load
error. The Component has errorString(); with no component the source is named.
Not reported upstream (the owner carries fixes here); drop this when upstream
fixes the handler.

Applied AFTER #1153 and #1155 in default.nix: its context is the tree those two
leave. --fuzz=0, so a reworded upstream block fails this build and says so.

diff --git a/shell/shell.qml b/shell/shell.qml
--- a/shell/shell.qml
+++ b/shell/shell.qml
@@ -1391,11 +1391,9 @@
         }
         onStatusChanged: {
           if (status === Loader.Error) {
-            // Loader.errorString() reflects the source-load failure even when
-            // sourceComponent is null. Surface both so the user sees something
-            // actionable instead of a panel that silently refuses to open.
-            var detail = errorString && errorString() ? errorString() : ""
-            if (!detail && sourceComponent) detail = sourceComponent.errorString()
+            // Qt 6's Loader has no errorString(); the Component does. With no
+            // component, name the source so the user still sees what failed.
+            var detail = sourceComponent ? sourceComponent.errorString() : String(source)
             console.warn("panel plugin " + panelEntry.pluginId + " failed to load:", detail)
             shell.hide(panelEntry.pluginId)
           }
